{"hash":"2a7daa4057cbae815de2a62d741445383ecdaeaf","data":{"metadata":{"siteName":"Emrah Korkmaz Bloggi","siteDescription":"Technology blog of myself; I write generally what I learned"},"post":{"id":"2c6e1af0c025687a404767dd7a200809","title":"Building a Blog with Gridsome & Publish it to Firebase / Github Pages","content":"<p>This is my first blog post on Github Pages and thanks to Gridsome. Gridsome is a Vue based static website generator library. It's a cool product which provides you make static websites with tons of starters. I used one of them. So let's start how can we build another one with it.</p>\n<p>First start with install Gridsome with shell command tools. I used all Gridsome works with it's cli. Install it with <code class=\"language-text\">yarn</code> or <code class=\"language-text\">npm</code> </p>\n<pre class=\"language-js\"><code class=\"language-js\">yarn global add @gridsome<span class=\"token operator\">/</span>cli\nnpm install <span class=\"token operator\">--</span>global @gridsome<span class=\"token operator\">/</span>cli</code></pre>\n<p>After the installing <code class=\"language-text\">Gridsome</code> let's start with a starters. </p>\n<p>For this tutorial I choose a simple and good-looking starter template as you look below.\nIt,s git link is: <code class=\"language-text\">https://gridsome.org/starters/gridsome-liebling-starter/</code></p>\n<p> <img class=\"g-image g-image--lazy g-image--loading\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml,%3csvg fill='none' viewBox='0 0 840 840' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' xmlns:xlink='http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink'%3e%3cdefs%3e%3cfilter id='__svg-blur-4ce4d7b50a328df2ad1c4a1c6e2023f2'%3e%3cfeGaussianBlur in='SourceGraphic' stdDeviation='40'/%3e%3c/filter%3e%3c/defs%3e%3cimage x='0' y='0' filter='url(%23__svg-blur-4ce4d7b50a328df2ad1c4a1c6e2023f2)' width='840' height='840' xlink:href='data:image/png%3bbase64%2ciVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAEAAAABACAIAAAAlC%2baJAAAACXBIWXMAABYlAAAWJQFJUiTwAAAIX0lEQVRo3u1Z6VMT2RbPXzJ/xXx5f8